BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:7c149708601b4aa1@zcyber-gtm.local
DTSTAMP:20260817T162520Z
DTSTART:20260819T120000Z
DTEND:20260819T133000Z
SUMMARY:(CS)²AI Author Spotlight™ on Matthew Luallen
DESCRIPTION:Nashville Cyber Security for Control Systems Matthew Luallen is the author of *What the Cursor Holds* and founder and principal advisor of Sph3r3\, LLC\, where he helps organizations adopt AI securely — treating security as the foundation\, not a feature — across cybersecurity strategy\, AI governance\, and cyber-physical systems. That perspective was built over three decades defending critical infrastructure. Matthew co-founded three companies in control system cybersecurity: Encari\, which guided North American power grid operators through NERC CIP\; Dragos Security\, where he helped create CyberLens for OT asset discovery\; and CYBATI\, the cyber-physical security training company later acquired by IntelliGenesis. Earlier\, he served as an information security engineer and architect at Argonne National Laboratory. A longtime SANS Institute certified instructor and now Lead Research Scientist for Education Translation at the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign's Information Trust Institute\, he has trained more than 9\,000 professionals across government\, utilities\, and industry. *What the Cursor Holds* turns that engineer's discipline inward. Built from 5\,775 logged AI conversations spanning 2022 to 2026\, it is a three-voice account — narrator\, machine\, and user — of the midnight conversations where people bring their work\, their questions\, and their most human moments to a machine that answers back. In this Author Series conversation\, Matthew explores the intersection where he has spent his career: people\, AI\, and cybersecurity for cyber-physical systems — and what keeping the human in the loop means when the loop is learning back. **[CLICK HERE TO REGISTER](https://events.zoom.us/ev/Apeq6RJSCfe-P88taFQtRoARELsOZ2elg3Ad2FeC8g-Taq3bGH1-~AlBj0W_uFRWfd7a5jv0a2_J-kXC-qA6_aTgusWGruIoov5t3MyO1pkXQD4DYouI-9U0kx-lD8oy9DvDqfBNwwe9p3w)** | Source: Nashville Cyber Security for Control Systems | Tags: cyber\, cybersecurity\, security | https://www.meetup.com/nashville-cyber-security-for-control-systems/events/315977642/
LOCATION:
URL:https://www.meetup.com/nashville-cyber-security-for-control-systems/events/315977642/
END:VEVENT
